The gate test's `crossPair` colour/class rows are a **sampler point emulation that does not read
buildTile colour/material bytes**. Its height rows do read buildTile. Consequently M0 does not move
any ceiling cell. The footprint report explicitly labels forest, name, carriedName and ocean as this
point emulation, because those labels are not stored per vertex. BEFORE=AFTER:

