Height retention uses a 129² grid over each of the same tiles, with 128 samples from each of its 129
rows and 129 columns. Spacing is tileEdge/128. `bandPowers` performs linear detrending and Hann
windowing; powers pool over rows, columns and tiles before taking ratios. The last spatial endpoint
is excluded from each FFT, not from the sampled grid. N=2*tileEdge/32. Values below are
**retained RMS / error power relative to truth**, BEFORE=AFTER: stored height buffers were compared
