316:### 2.0 M0: coarse reduction (LOD precondition, comes first)
317-
318-- **What.** Coarse colour texels and class-lattice weights become the footprint mean of K x K
319-  sub-samples (K=2 measured as enough) at the levels where it measurably helps. In the proxy that
320-  is L6; L8 got slightly worse. The level rule (L <= `peakCorrectionMaxLevel(R)`, or narrower) is set
321-  by measurement in `buildTile`, not in the proxy. Heights keep the point sample plus the existing peak correction; the contract says
322-  heights are only raised.
323-- Each terrain band declares its shortest wavelength (see M2 and M3). The ladder can then report, per
324-  level, which bands sit below Nyquist(L).
325-- **Owner files:** `src/planet-tiles.ts` (colour and class grid hunks only), `src/lod-ladder.ts`
326-  (reduction constants, `LOD_LADDER_VERSION` lod-ladder-2), `scripts/lod-consistency-report.mjs`
327-  (footprint mode), `tests/lod-consistency.test.mjs` (ceilings, changed only after the owner's A3
328-  answer), and the new `tests/lod-footprint.test.mjs`.
329-- **Metrics and thresholds:**
330-  1. *Structural (unit, exact):* on a synthetic colour field, a coarse texel equals the mean of its
331-     K² sub-samples, bit-identical across visit order and processes.
332-  2. *Reduction on main's own field (integration):* L6 RGB p99 at most 0.9 x the point value on
333-     both Maithea and Lethuris, measured through `buildTile`. Proxy measurement: 0.86 and 0.67 at
334-     K=2. The 0.9 leaves margin and still demands a real effect.
335-  3. *Per-octave height retention*, on the coarse surface interpolated at a 4x denser grid against
336-     the truth, octave by octave from the shared spectrum function:
337-     - a retained RMS ratio of at least 0.9 for wavelengths of 4 Nyquist(L) or more;
338-     - error power at most 0.25 of the truth power in the octave just above Nyquist(L), which is
339-       what a coarse level may get wrong.
340-
341-     These two are proposed bounds, not measured; MTN-1 measures them on main first and records the
342-     values before fixing the thresholds.
343-  4. *Cost (benchmark):* build mean at most +10% per level (`LOD_BUDGETS.buildTimeGrowth`). Measure
344-     K=2 against K=1. If it is over, apply the footprint only to the colour grid at L <= 7.
345-- **Single-element render:** a coarse-against-child |RGB| difference heat map per level (PNG from
346-  Node), point and footprint side by side, on the 12 test tiles.
347-- **Must not depend on:** any mountain element, or the tile selection of a candidate field. The unit
348-  test must not depend on the climate colour constants either. The integration check runs on
349-  main's field, so M0 lands before any terrain change.
350-
